import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,ak as r}from"./chunks/framework.B8jO0odJ.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Chainy hardware baseline and validation","description":"Capstone project title: Chainy: A 3D World Educational Game for learning emerging Technology (Blockchain & AI)","frontmatter":{"title":"Chainy hardware baseline and validation","description":"Capstone project title: Chainy: A 3D World Educational Game for learning emerging Technology (Blockchain & AI)","source":"docs/hardware-validation.md","category":"Research & evaluation","sourceUpdated":"2026-10-08T07:30:14+08:00","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"content/docs/hardware-validation.md","filePath":"content/docs/hardware-validation.md"}'),n={name:"content/docs/hardware-validation.md"};function o(s,e,d,l,c,p){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<div><h1 id="chainy-hardware-baseline-and-validation">Chainy hardware baseline and validation<a class="header-anchor" href="#chainy-hardware-baseline-and-validation" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h1><p><strong>Capstone project title:</strong> Chainy: A 3D World Educational Game for learning emerging Technology (Blockchain &amp; AI)</p><p>Mentor verdict: <strong>validate first</strong>. On October 8 the user explicitly retained the target specification: Android 10+/11+, 4 GB RAM, 64 GB total device storage, a 64-bit ARM CPU, OpenGL ES 3.2 or Vulkan 1.1, and an entry-level-to-midrange GPU. Preserve these stated specs in the GDD. They are a target device class, not a measured minimum or compatibility guarantee.</p><h2 id="working-interpretation">Working interpretation<a class="header-anchor" href="#working-interpretation" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Planning baseline</th><th>What must be verified</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Android</td><td>Recommend 11+ for the initial pilot; 10 is a candidate compatibility test</td><td>Exact minimum API selected in the pinned Unity build and tested on a real device</td></tr><tr><td>RAM</td><td>4 GB physical RAM candidate</td><td>Measure app memory and sustained performance with typical background load; do not count virtual/extended RAM as physical</td></tr><tr><td>Storage</td><td>64 GB total device capacity is the proposed device class</td><td>Installation needs available space, not a 64 GB allocation; proposed 2 GB free for install/update/export headroom</td></tr><tr><td>CPU/OS</td><td>ARM64 with a 64-bit OS/runtime</td><td>Actual Android ABI and selected Unity/SQLite native libraries</td></tr><tr><td>Graphics</td><td>User retains OpenGL ES 3.2 or Vulkan 1.1; either capability meets the stated target</td><td>Select and record the actual rendering path during the device spike; driver/API compatibility still requires testing</td></tr><tr><td>GPU</td><td>No universal performance meaning for entry-level-to-midrange</td><td>Record actual SoC/GPU and test the representative/worst activity</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Unity&#39;s <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/system-requirements.html">6.0 platform requirements</a> list ARM64 and OpenGL ES 3.0+/Vulkan support for Android. Those are engine capabilities, not evidence that Chainy performs well on every supported device. Recheck documentation for the exact Unity version selected in CH-03. Do not copy embedded-Linux Vulkan requirements into an Android claim.</p><p>The 64 GB figure describes total device capacity, not a request for the game to occupy 64 GB. Retain it in the target specification and separately measure installation, update and export space. A support claim requires actual test evidence.</p><h2 id="proposed-engineering-targets">Proposed engineering targets<a class="header-anchor" href="#proposed-engineering-targets" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><p>These are initial budgets to challenge in the first spike, not achieved measurements or school requirements.</p><ul><li>Target 30 FPS during a sustained representative session. Record average, p95 frame time and visible stalls; proposed p95 frame-time target at most 40 ms.</li><li>Test for 15 minutes minimum across the world map, bounded ordering/linking, three local replicas and AI activity; then run a full session for thermal/battery observation. The approved direct lesson navigation supersedes exploration and free-construction performance scenarios.</li><li>Proposed process-memory budget: at most 800 MiB total PSS on the candidate 4 GB device. Record the measurement method and build type; Unity allocations and Android process PSS are different metrics.</li><li>Proposed APK budget: at most 500 MB. Record installed size separately. Proposed cold start at most 15 seconds and ordinary scene transition at most 8 seconds on the baseline device.</li><li>Save/submit actions must not lose committed data or freeze the interaction; measure durations rather than assuming SQLite is free.</li><li>Visual simplification precedes removing required learning behavior: reduce texture sizes/effects, visible props and shadow cost first.</li></ul><p>Use simple shaders, shared materials, modest textures, bounded particles and collision shapes. Start with a compact scene; measure before adding batching/culling systems. Choose compression supported by tested devices instead of mandating ASTC universally.</p><h2 id="spike-and-device-record">Spike and device record<a class="header-anchor" href="#spike-and-device-record" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><p>Christian owns CH-03/04; Luis provides a deliberately small representative asset sample; Miguel provides a readable HUD; Sherwin reviews the decision. Limit initial adapter/build exploration to two focused days before explicitly escalating a blocker.</p><p>Pass: APK installs and works in airplane mode, touch controls respond, SQLite persists two profiles, export produces a readable file, and basic render/memory metrics are recorded. Fail: document exact adapter/build/device error and select a narrower compatible path; do not assert feasibility from the editor.</p><p>For each device record model, manufacturer, Android version, physical RAM, free storage, SoC/GPU, ABI, graphics API actually used, resolution, build commit/version, build settings, thermal conditions and test workload. No available models have yet been provided.</p><p>Coverage target: one candidate 4 GB baseline phone, one weaker or Android 10 candidate if available, and one newer comparison device. The weaker device is exploratory unless added to supported scope after passing. The absence of test hardware is a risk owned by Sherwin, not a reason to declare arbitrary minimums.</p><p>Release support statements must list tested device/build combinations and limitations. Android 10 support remains undecided until validated; Android 11+ is the provisional documentation baseline.</p></div>',1)])])}const u=t(n,[["render",o]]);export{m as __pageData,u as default};
